    "body": "Line: cross-state continuation / bank-mixture configuration · count 1/3 unchanged · headline dev437/512 + fresh0/128 → dev437/512 + fresh0/128.\n\nThe owner replaced the active goal with D22 while the registered bank-mixture run was replaying its baseline. Preserve that work as **UNFINISHED_NOT_NEGATIVE** and clear the way for the ordered constructor repair. The run was interrupted at zero optimizer updates, with checkpoint0000 and512+128 baseline row files, but no trained endpoint or terminal seal. No KEEP, negative count or mechanism closure is claimed.\n\nThe complete producer changes are retained as a restorable patch and INDEX row; active Rust source is byte-identical to the base main. The canonical record binds source, data, checks, interruption and the verified20.48MB iCloud package. README's How it works and Results so far, STATUS, ROADMAP and current-state now reflect D22's reopened constructor/joint-learning orders and label437/512 with0/128 fresh as panel fitting. Own GPU lease is released and pod deleted.\n\n“If this came out the other way, would my next step differ?” This is required preservation of in-flight work under the owner's goal replacement, not an experiment or substitute scientific deliverable. Failed source/evidence verification would block cleanup and constructor work; the verified archive permits the ordered repair. The superseded experiment's registered opposite outcomes would have led to fresh qualification versus rejecting its mixture recipe, but neither outcome was measured.\n\nValidation at exact head401374bfb3ed8bcd8285dfd49f1b61a5db9936ab: patch application check PASS; active crates equal base4ae040cb2; claim-wording gate PASS; non-patch diff whitespace check PASS. Literal unified-diff context spaces in the archived patch are preserved. The producer had52 preparation and34 fitter focused checks PASS and a successful CUDA build before launch; these are preparation evidence, not tests of an activated delivery or a capability result. Exact-head self-review found no unsupported KEEP/negative or missing preservation boundary.\n\nReferences #2030. The continuous D22 goal remains active; constructor pivot repair and native512/fresh128 scoring follow verified merge and cleanup, then the ordered joint Context–prototype intervention.\n",
